WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.700
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:12.370
Last time: guess → check → improve

3
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:19.450
Chapter 2 · Probability

4
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:29.830
Probability = chance. How likely is it?

5
00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:37.620
Meet Aarav, playing Ludo with Nani

6
00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:45.660
"Please be a six!"

7
00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:54.380
A six on the first roll? Think!

8
00:00:54.380 --> 00:01:08.530
Nobody knows for sure, but we know how likely

9
00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:15.980
Probability = the chance something happens

10
00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:27.270
Impossible → Unlikely → Likely → Certain

11
00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:39.680
Never · Probably not · Probably · Surely

12
00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:47.440
The sun will rise tomorrow → certain

13
00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:57.480
Roll a 7 on a normal die → impossible

14
00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:08.830
A 6 on the first roll: 1 out of 6 → unlikely

15
00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:20.090
Smaller than 6: 5 out of 6 → likely

16
00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:28.550
The cricket toss: heads or tails?

17
00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:37.460
Heads: 1 out of 2 · Tails: 1 out of 2

18
00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:49.650
Lots of tosses → about half and half

19
00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:57.630
Fair = every result has the same chance

20
00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:04.800
6 faces · each number is 1 out of 6

21
00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:15.340
Chance of an even number? Count!

22
00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:26.000
Even: 2, 4, 6 → 3 out of 6

23
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:34.510
7 blue marbles and 3 yellow marbles

24
00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:46.150
Chance of yellow? Likely or unlikely?

25
00:03:46.150 --> 00:04:02.690
Yellow: 3 out of 10 · Blue: 7 out of 10

26
00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:16.430
No red marbles → red is impossible

27
00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:28.020
4 equal parts → fair

28
00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:38.420
3 red, 1 blue → red is more likely

29
00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:48.560
One part is half the circle. Fair?

30
00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:58.140
Not fair! Fair spinners have equal parts

31
00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:02.340
AI uses chance too!

32
00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:12.110
Seen lots of cats → pointy ears? Likely a cat

33
00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:21.280
"Happy…" → "birthday" is most likely

34
00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:30.830
Most likely is not certain. AI can be wrong!

35
00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:34.530
Your turn: practice check

36
00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:46.220
Rolling a 7: impossible or unlikely? Why?

37
00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:58.360
Impossible! A die only has 1 to 6

38
00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:05.300
Impossible → unlikely → likely → certain

39
00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:09.250
Coin: heads and tails equally likely

40
00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:15.650
Fair = every result, same chance

41
00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:20.020
AI picks the most likely, from examples

42
00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:25.530
Chapter 2 done!

43
00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:32.330
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
